      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg in one dose is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this level:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove these risks.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum anti-inflammatory dose, for example in rheumatologic conditions.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO twice daily.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed** for pain or fever.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that you do intend 1600 mg four times daily. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note recording that it was intentional. I can also add a note about GI protection or duration if you'd like."
      }
